WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.750
MedlinePlus is the National Library of Medicine's consumer

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.800
health resource designed specifically for caregivers,

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.000
patients, and family members.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.500
The scenario you are about to view is just one of the many

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.950
ways MedlinePlus can be used.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.900
Michelle's mother, Vivian, was diagnosed this year with

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.650
Alzheimer's disease.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.000
Even though Michelle had read and heard about Alzheimer's

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.700
disease, she wanted to learn more about the disease

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.500
and possible treatments.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.500
As her mother's primary caregiver,

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.900
Michelle also understands the importance of maintaining

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.350
her own health.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.300
A librarian friend suggested that Michelle go online to the

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:38.800
National Library of Medicine's website, medlineplus.gov.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.900
These pages are a great place to start when looking for quality

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.000
health information you can trust.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:47.150
The MedlinePlus homepage provides an outline of all the

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.000
information the website has to offer.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.000
Displayed at the top of the screen are new and

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.000
featured health topics.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.600
Michelle clicked on the ESPANOL button and was pleased to find

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.200
the site was also available in Spanish.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.700
She wanted to return to the English version of the site,

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.200
so she clicked on the ENGLISH button.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.200
A little further down on the homepage,

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:05.400
there are three tabs that link to the Health Topics,

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:09.700
Drugs and Supplements and Videos and Cool Tools sections.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:13.200
The tabs are located on every MedlinePlus page.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:16.250
Michelle can also search each of these categories by using the

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.750
Search box at the top of each page.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.300
The Health Topics section provides information on

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:24.750
disorders and conditions, diagnosis and therapy,

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.800
health and wellness, and population groups.

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.750
The Drugs and Supplements section offers information on

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.700
prescription drugs, over-the-counter medicines,

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:36.800
dietary supplements, and herbal remedies.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:40.150
The Videos and Cool Tools section provides videos and

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.250
interactive tutorials about medical conditions, treatments,

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.200
and procedures as well as anatomy and surgery videos.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.900
The Medical Dictionary is very useful in helping Michelle

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:51.950
understand medical terms.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.250
Michelle learns something new every time she visits the

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.200
MedlinePlus website.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.200
Helpful new information on the homepage banner always

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:00.900
catches her attention.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:03.500
At the bottom of the page, Michelle discovered links to

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:06.650
Directories for locating libraries, health professionals,

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:10.400
and services; Organizations with health information;

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:13.600
and a Medical Encyclopedia with illustrated articles about

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.200
diseases, tests, and symptoms.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.800
Health News is a convenient way for Michelle to read press

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:21.750
announcements from major health organizations.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:24.600
Michelle also noted that she could register to receive email

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:27.750
updates when new information is available on Alzheimer's disease

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:30.150
and other health topics of interest to her.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:33.300
Michelle was also very excited to see that a Mobile version of

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:36.800
MedlinePlus was available to use on her smartphone.

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:40.200
This concludes the MedlinePlus homepage scenario.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.500
Whether you are a caregiver, patient, or family member,

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:45.950
we hope that you have found this information useful.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.750
For additional information, please visit MedlinePlus.gov.

